[DOCUMENT]
MID: 3a86b0c4bd134cc7b7609077f2d20a62
TITLE: Domain: motor control
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 8e4b2643b44749f69d92bdca3971d262
UID: SWR-CTL-001
TITLE: Setpoint clamp and ramp
STATEMENT: >>>
``motor_control_set_speed`` shall clamp the target to
``[-max_setpoint_rpm, max_setpoint_rpm]``. Each ``motor_control_step`` call
shall move the ramped setpoint toward the target by at most
``ramp_rpm_per_tick``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 82015a97d2fa480b87fd0085d427b8ec
UID: SWR-CTL-002
TITLE: Drive disabled outside RUNNING
STATEMENT: >>>
In every state other than ``RUNNING``, ``motor_control_step`` shall return a
drive command with ``enable = false`` and ``duty = 0``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 678ecdbb09b64ed3ad47717656892213
UID: SWR-CTL-003
TITLE: Bumpless start
STATEMENT: >>>
On entering ``RUNNING``, the controller shall reset the PI controller and start
the ramped setpoint at the measured speed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Starting the ramp at the measured speed avoids a step in duty when the operator
restarts a motor that is still coasting.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-001

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 5aecd275fad547c0a9caecf0e8127258
UID: SWR-CTL-004
TITLE: Same-step fault shutdown
STATEMENT: >>>
When the fault monitor reports a fault, ``motor_control_step`` shall latch the
fault flags, move the state machine to ``FAULT``, and return a disabled drive
command in that same call. ``CLEAR_FAULT`` shall clear the latched flags.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-004
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-005
